    {
      "id": "TBT19qlxfAA-kC9cjLzKQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5672.414579235251,
      "y": 2672.2879411633908,
      "width": 486.38567926023967,
      "height": 38.50183624972988,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1929618954,
      "version": 106,
      "versionNonce": 1821473302,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791414577523,
      "created": 1791413190589,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Back of the envelope estimation",
      "fontSize": 30.801468999783904,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Back of the envelope estimation",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8Jds8n_gsUfDTYXCyf9ZO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5501.25391604314,
      "y": 2791.3402914149847,
      "width": 944.4696066677757,
      "height": 1270.560596241086,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1446505558,
      "version": 1505,
      "versionNonce": 2143668054,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791414577523,
      "created": 1791413207795,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Uber has 6M drivers\n3M of them are active at a given time\nDriver sends location update every 5 second\n=>3M/5 = 600k Transactions per second (TPA)\n\nUsing postgres:\n(lat, long) up down left right -> basically box the pickup\nlocation\nSince postgres uses binary index trees, it is good at indexing\none  dimensional data.\nSo now we need to scan a tonne of rows!!\nAlso postgres can handle 2-4k TPA normally[way off]\nSo postgres is a TERRIBLE CHOICE!!\n\nTo handle location search, introduce GEOSPATIAL INDEX\nwhich uses QUAD-TREE. Postgres has POSTGIS.\n\nNow to handle increased transaction, introduce a QUEUE. \nBut a queue will introduce batching, which will affect latency. \nAlso every time location data is  put, we need to re-index our\nQuad-tree.\n\nSOLUTION:\nUse Redis\nRedis supports GeoHashing out of the box\nIt just produces a hashed string which is a lot easier to\nstore and query for. It is easier to calculate as well. It\ndoesn't require any special structure. \n\nRedis also supports 100k-1M TPS\nUber uses Geohashing, but instead of them being squares, it's\nactually hexagons.\n",
      "fontSize": 30.801468999783904,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Uber has 6M drivers\n3M of them are active at a given time\nDriver sends location update every 5 second\n=>3M/5 = 600k Transactions per second (TPA)\n\nUsing postgres:\n(lat, long) up down left right -> basically box the pickup location\nSince postgres uses binary index trees, it is good at indexing one  dimensional data.\nSo now we need to scan a tonne of rows!!\nAlso postgres can handle 2-4k TPA normally[way off]\nSo postgres is a TERRIBLE CHOICE!!\n\nTo handle location search, introduce GEOSPATIAL INDEX which uses QUAD-TREE. Postgres has POSTGIS.\n\nNow to handle increased transaction, introduce a QUEUE. \nBut a queue will introduce batching, which will affect latency. \nAlso every time location data is  put, we need to re-index our Quad-tree.\n\nSOLUTION:\nUse Redis\nRedis supports GeoHashing out of the box\nIt just produces a hashed string which is a lot easier to store and query for. It is easier to calculate as well. It doesn't require any special structure. \n\nRedis also supports 100k-1M TPS\nUber uses Geohashing, but instead of them being squares, it's actually hexagons.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
