      "text": "Consistency of Matching",
      "fontSize": 30.801468999783904,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Consistency of Matching",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bmA2AOHQ19aqJAoklFFN_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11672.723528446993,
      "y": 3531.96817488437,
      "width": 944.4696066677757,
      "height": 693.0330524951378,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 824177366,
      "version": 2637,
      "versionNonce": 955893002,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "8m3Wt5wCcWjdPE4XXuhno",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1791415928160,
      "created": 1791415005790,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. We don't send more than one request at a time for a given\nride\n\n2. We don't send any driver more than one request at a time\n\n3. Drivers who are sent request are locked for a period of\ntime (5 seconds to accept it and its status will be changed\nto request_sent)\n\n4. We can have a regular cron job to be updating the status\nof the driver from request_sent back to available. But this\napproach would introduce a delta n. \n\n5. So just like ticket master we can use a DISTrIBUTED\nLOCK\n\n6. OR you can use a Dyanamo DB, which allows for TTL, so\nyou won't need a separate REDIS just for distributed lock",
      "fontSize": 30.801468999783904,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. We don't send more than one request at a time for a given ride\n\n2. We don't send any driver more than one request at a time\n\n3. Drivers who are sent request are locked for a period of time (5 seconds to accept it and its status will be changed to request_sent)\n\n4. We can have a regular cron job to be updating the status of the driver from request_sent back to available. But this approach would introduce a delta n. \n\n5. So just like ticket master we can use a DISTrIBUTED LOCK\n\n6. OR you can use a Dyanamo DB, which allows for TTL, so you won't need a separate REDIS just for distributed lock",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
